1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,420
Slaves built the pyramids... or did they?

2
00:00:03,840 --> 00:00:07,890
This carving in an Egyptian temple seems
to show a helicopter.

3
00:00:08,090 --> 00:00:13,090
In 1968, a Swiss writer said ancient
astronauts had visited Egypt.

4
00:00:13,290 --> 00:00:15,300
His followers saw more clues.

5
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:18,920
At Dendera, a snake in what looks like a
giant bulb.

6
00:00:19,120 --> 00:00:22,100
At Saqqara, a wooden bird with glider
wings.

7
00:00:22,300 --> 00:00:26,260
And the Great Pyramid: about 2.3 million
blocks.

8
00:00:26,320 --> 00:00:28,360
Some claim it was a power plant.

9
00:00:28,560 --> 00:00:32,460
Others, a stargate: one shaft once aimed
at Orion's belt.

10
00:00:32,780 --> 00:00:34,710
Or so the story goes.

11
00:00:35,080 --> 00:00:38,200
In 1990, a horse tripped on a buried wall.

12
00:00:38,250 --> 00:00:42,240
Beneath it lay the builders, buried with
honor, not as slaves.

13
00:00:42,420 --> 00:00:45,720
Their gangs signed the stones: Friends of
Khufu.

14
00:00:45,920 --> 00:00:47,250
Drunkards of Menkaure.

15
00:00:47,450 --> 00:00:51,120
A papyrus logbook tracks boats of
limestone to Giza.

16
00:00:51,320 --> 00:00:54,130
Yet the king's sarcophagus was found
empty.

17
00:00:54,330 --> 00:00:59,580
Later pyramid texts promise the king a
staircase to the sky, to become Orion.

18
00:00:59,780 --> 00:01:02,500
A tomb... or a stairway to the stars?

19
00:01:02,820 --> 00:01:07,300
So... what do you think the pyramids
really were?
